module

public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.Smooth
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Divisors.EffectiveCartier

/-!
# The closed subscheme cut out by one global section

Let `Y` be a scheme and `a ∈ Γ(Y, ⊤)` a global section. The closed subscheme `V(a)` is
represented by `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop (Ideal.span {a})`, and this
file computes the two elementary invariants of that ideal sheaf data: the ideal it cuts out on
an arbitrary affine open, and its support.

The intended consumer is a *principal slice* of a morphism `f : X ⟶ S` through a point: an
affine open `U ∋ x`, a section `a ∈ Γ(X, U)` whose germ at `x` is a prescribed element `h` of
the maximal ideal of `𝒪_{X,x}`, and the subscheme of `U` cut out by `a`. Tags 056Y and 057C
both ask for such a slice, with the further requirements that it be an effective Cartier
divisor and that it be flat, respectively smooth, over `S`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Divisors.ideal_ofIdealTop_span_singleton`: the ideal cut out on an affine open `V` by
  `V(a)` is generated by the restriction of `a` to `V`.
* `Stacks.Divisors.eq_ofIdealTop_span_singleton`: conversely, an ideal sheaf data cutting out
  the restrictions of `a` on every affine open *is* `V(a)`. So the displayed family of
  principal ideals in Tags 056Y and 057C determines the subscheme, rather than merely
  constraining it.
* `Stacks.Divisors.mem_support_ofIdealTop_span_singleton_iff`: a point lies in the support of
  `V(a)` exactly when the germ of `a` there is not a unit.
* `Stacks.Divisors.exists_isAffineOpen_germ_eq`: every element of a stalk is the germ of a
  section on some *affine* open neighbourhood.
* `Stacks.Divisors.exists_isAffineOpen_principal_slice`: the three conjuncts of Tag 057C that
  need no hypothesis on `f` — the section realizing the germ, the principal ideals, and the
  point lying on the slice.
* `Stacks.Divisors.exists_principal_slice_iff`: the conclusion of Tag 057C is *equivalent* to
  its first, third and fifth conjuncts. The ideal computation and the support membership are
  free, so the whole content of that tag is "an effective Cartier divisor, smooth over `S`".

## Implementation notes

The support computation is stated with `IsUnit` of the germ rather than with membership in the
maximal ideal of the stalk, because `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.mem_basicOpen` is phrased that
way and the two are interchanged by `IsLocalRing.mem_maximalIdeal`.

The slice lives on `U.toScheme`, whose global sections are `Γ(X, U)` only up to the
isomorphism `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Opens.topIso`. Every statement below therefore applies
`U.topIso.inv` to the section of `X`, matching the companion statements; the transport of the
support computation across that isomorphism is
`Stacks.Divisors.mem_support_ofIdealTop_span_topIso_inv_iff`, which goes through the image
formula `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Opens.ι_image_basicOpen_topIso_inv` rather than through the
stalk isomorphism.

Neither the effective Cartier condition nor smoothness of the slice is proved here. Both are
genuinely missing from the repository: the first needs the nonzerodivisor criterion of Tag
01WS, whose two directions pass through the descent step recorded as unproved in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/InvertibleLocallyFree/Basic.lean`, and the second needs the
conormal exact sequence of Tag 01UZ together with the generator criterion of Tag 01V9.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 057C](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/057C)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 056Y](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/056Y)
-/

@[expose] public section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory TopologicalSpace Opposite

universe u

namespace Stacks.Divisors

/-- Two ideal sheaf data with the same ideals are equal: `ideal` is a left inverse of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdeals`. -/
theorem idealSheafData_ext {Y : Scheme.{u}} {I J : Y.IdealSheafData}
    (h : I.ideal = J.ideal) : I = J := by
  rw [← Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdeals_ideal I, ← Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdeals_ideal J, h]

/-- The subscheme cut out by a single global section `a` cuts out, on every affine open, the
principal ideal generated by the restriction of `a`. -/
theorem ideal_ofIdealTop_span_singleton {Y : Scheme.{u}} (a : Γ(Y, ⊤)) (V : Y.affineOpens) :
    (Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop (Ideal.span {a})).ideal V =
      Ideal.span {(Y.presheaf.map (homOfLE le_top).op).hom a} := by
  rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop_ideal, Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton]

/-- An ideal sheaf data whose ideal on every affine open is generated by the restriction of the
global section `a` is the subscheme cut out by `a`. -/
theorem eq_ofIdealTop_span_singleton {Y : Scheme.{u}} (a : Γ(Y, ⊤)) (I : Y.IdealSheafData)
    (h : ∀ V : Y.affineOpens,
      I.ideal V = Ideal.span {(Y.presheaf.map (homOfLE le_top).op).hom a}) :
    I = Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop (Ideal.span {a}) :=
  idealSheafData_ext (funext fun V => (h V).trans (ideal_ofIdealTop_span_singleton a V).symm)

/-- A point lies in the support of the subscheme cut out by a global section exactly when the
germ of that section at the point is not a unit. -/
theorem mem_support_ofIdealTop_span_singleton_iff {Y : Scheme.{u}} (a : Γ(Y, ⊤)) (y : Y) :
    y ∈ (Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop (Ideal.span {a})).support ↔
      ¬ IsUnit ((Y.presheaf.germ ⊤ y trivial).hom a) := by
  obtain ⟨V, hyV⟩ : ∃ V : Y.affineOpens, y ∈ (V : Set Y) := exists_affineOpens_mem y
  rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.mem_support_iff_of_mem hyV,
    ideal_ofIdealTop_span_singleton a ⟨V, V.2⟩, Scheme.zeroLocus_span,
    Scheme.zeroLocus_singleton, Set.mem_compl_iff, SetLike.mem_coe,
    Y.mem_basicOpen _ y hyV, TopCat.Presheaf.germ_res_apply]

/-- A point of an open subscheme lies in the basic open of the transported section exactly when
the corresponding point of the ambient scheme lies in the basic open of the section. -/
theorem mem_basicOpen_topIso_inv_iff {X : Scheme.{u}} (U : X.Opens) (a : Γ(X, U)) (x : X)
    (hxU : x ∈ U) :
    (⟨x, hxU⟩ : U.toScheme) ∈ U.toScheme.basicOpen (U.topIso.inv.hom a) ↔ x ∈ X.basicOpen a := by
  rw [← Scheme.Opens.ι_image_basicOpen_topIso_inv (U := U) a]
  refine ⟨fun hy => ⟨⟨x, hxU⟩, hy, rfl⟩, ?_⟩
  rintro ⟨⟨y, hyU⟩, hy, rfl⟩
  exact hy

/-- The support computation of `Stacks.Divisors.mem_support_ofIdealTop_span_singleton_iff`,
transported to the slice of an open subscheme: the point of `U` corresponding to `x` lies on the
subscheme cut out by `a` exactly when the germ of `a` at `x` is not a unit. -/
theorem mem_support_ofIdealTop_span_topIso_inv_iff {X : Scheme.{u}} (U : X.Opens) (a : Γ(X, U))
    (x : X) (hxU : x ∈ U) :
    (⟨x, hxU⟩ : U.toScheme) ∈
        (Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop (Ideal.span {U.topIso.inv.hom a})).support ↔
      ¬ IsUnit ((X.presheaf.germ U x hxU).hom a) :=
  (mem_support_ofIdealTop_span_singleton_iff (U.topIso.inv.hom a) ⟨x, hxU⟩).trans
    (not_congr
      ((U.toScheme.mem_basicOpen (U.topIso.inv.hom a) ⟨x, hxU⟩ trivial).symm.trans
        ((mem_basicOpen_topIso_inv_iff U a x hxU).trans (X.mem_basicOpen a x hxU))))

/-- A point of an open subscheme lies on the subscheme cut out by a section whose germ at the
point lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk. -/
private theorem mem_support_ofIdealTop_span_topIso_inv_of_mem_maximalIdeal {X : Scheme.{u}}
    (U : X.Opens) (a : Γ(X, U)) (x : X) (hxU : x ∈ U)
    {h : X.presheaf.stalk x} (ha : (X.presheaf.germ U x hxU).hom a = h)
    (hh : h ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk x)) :
    (⟨x, hxU⟩ : U.toScheme) ∈
      (Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop (Ideal.span {U.topIso.inv.hom a})).support :=
  (mem_support_ofIdealTop_span_topIso_inv_iff U a x hxU).mpr
    ((IsLocalRing.mem_maximalIdeal _).mp (ha ▸ hh))

/-- Every element of a stalk is the germ of a section on an affine open neighbourhood: a
representative on an arbitrary open restricts to one on an affine open of the basis. -/
theorem exists_isAffineOpen_germ_eq {X : Scheme.{u}} (x : X) (h : X.presheaf.stalk x) :
    ∃ (U : X.Opens) (_ : IsAffineOpen U) (hxU : x ∈ U) (a : Γ(X, U)),
      (X.presheaf.germ U x hxU).hom a = h := by
  obtain ⟨W, hxW, s, hs⟩ := X.presheaf.exists_germ_eq h
  obtain ⟨_, ⟨V, hV, rfl⟩, hxV, hVW⟩ :=
    X.isBasis_affineOpens.exists_subset_of_mem_open hxW W.2
  exact ⟨V, hV, hxV, (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (show V ≤ W from hVW)).op).hom s,
    (X.presheaf.germ_res_apply (homOfLE (show V ≤ W from hVW)) x hxV s).trans hs⟩

/-- **The hypothesis-free part of Stacks Project, Tag 057C.** An element of the maximal ideal of
a stalk is the germ of a section `a` on an affine open neighbourhood `U`, the subscheme of `U`
cut out by `a` cuts out the principal ideals generated by the restrictions of `a`, and the point
lies on that subscheme.

These are the first, second and fourth conjuncts of Tag 057C. Nothing about a morphism out of
`X` enters, and no smoothness or finiteness hypothesis is used. -/
theorem exists_isAffineOpen_principal_slice {X : Scheme.{u}} (x : X) (h : X.presheaf.stalk x)
    (hh : h ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk x)) :
    ∃ (U : X.Opens) (_ : IsAffineOpen U) (hxU : x ∈ U) (a : Γ(X, U)),
      (X.presheaf.germ U x hxU).hom a = h ∧
      (∀ V : U.toScheme.affineOpens,
        (Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop (Ideal.span {U.topIso.inv.hom a})).ideal V =
          Ideal.span {((U.toScheme.presheaf.map (homOfLE le_top).op).hom
            (U.topIso.inv.hom a))}) ∧
      (⟨x, hxU⟩ : U.toScheme) ∈
        (Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop (Ideal.span {U.topIso.inv.hom a})).support := by
  obtain ⟨U, hU, hxU, a, ha⟩ := exists_isAffineOpen_germ_eq x h
  exact ⟨U, hU, hxU, a, ha, ideal_ofIdealTop_span_singleton _,
    mem_support_ofIdealTop_span_topIso_inv_of_mem_maximalIdeal U a x hxU ha hh⟩

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 057C, reduced to its own first, third and fifth conjuncts.** The
conclusion of Tag 057C holds if and only if there are an affine open `U ∋ x` and a section `a`
on `U` with germ `h` at `x` such that the subscheme of `U` cut out by `a` is an effective
Cartier divisor smooth over `S`.

The two directions say different things. From left to right, the family of principal ideals in
Tag 057C pins the ideal sheaf data down to `V(a)`, by
`Stacks.Divisors.eq_ofIdealTop_span_singleton`; so no generality is lost by naming the
subscheme. From right to left, the ideal computation and the support membership come for free,
by `Stacks.Divisors.exists_isAffineOpen_principal_slice`. The equivalence is therefore an exact
accounting of what Tag 057C still demands, and it demands only the two conjuncts that mention
the morphism. -/
theorem exists_principal_slice_iff {X S : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ S) (x : X)
    (h : X.presheaf.stalk x) (hh : h ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk x)) :
    (∃ (U : X.Opens) (_ : IsAffineOpen U) (hxU : x ∈ U) (a : Γ(X, U))
        (I : U.toScheme.IdealSheafData),
        (X.presheaf.germ U x hxU).hom a = h ∧
        (∀ V : U.toScheme.affineOpens,
          I.ideal V = Ideal.span {((U.toScheme.presheaf.map (homOfLE le_top).op).hom
            (U.topIso.inv.hom a))}) ∧
        IsEffectiveCartierDivisor I ∧
        (⟨x, hxU⟩ : U.toScheme) ∈ I.support ∧
        Smooth (I.subschemeι ≫ U.ι ≫ f)) ↔
      (∃ (U : X.Opens) (_ : IsAffineOpen U) (hxU : x ∈ U) (a : Γ(X, U)),
        (X.presheaf.germ U x hxU).hom a = h ∧
        IsEffectiveCartierDivisor
          (Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop (Ideal.span {U.topIso.inv.hom a})) ∧
        Smooth ((Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop
          (Ideal.span {U.topIso.inv.hom a})).subschemeι ≫ U.ι ≫ f)) := by
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨U, hU, hxU, a, I, ha, hideal, hEC, -, hsm⟩
    obtain rfl := eq_ofIdealTop_span_singleton _ I hideal
    exact ⟨U, hU, hxU, a, ha, hEC, hsm⟩
  · rintro ⟨U, hU, hxU, a, ha, hEC, hsm⟩
    exact ⟨U, hU, hxU, a, _, ha, ideal_ofIdealTop_span_singleton _, hEC,
      mem_support_ofIdealTop_span_topIso_inv_of_mem_maximalIdeal U a x hxU ha hh, hsm⟩

end Stacks.Divisors

end
